@owner: mason
@stability: stable
@since: 2026-06-10
@reviewed: 2026-06-10

Feature: Doctor Command
  "CLI handler for mason doctor: run read-only target diagnostics and exit non-zero when a check fails."

  Provides:
    - cli.newDoctorCommand @source("symbol:newDoctorCommand")
    - cli.defaultDoctorRun @source("symbol:defaultDoctorRun")

  Consumes:
    - setup.Diagnose
    - setup.DoctorDeps
    - remote.SSHOptionsFromTarget
    - remote.NewSSH
    - remote.NewSSHFS
    - remote.NewRemoteManifestStore
    - output.WriteJSON

  Invariants:
    - The command MUST render the full report before exiting non-zero on failed checks
    - Warnings MUST exit zero; only fail status drives a non-zero exit
    - JSON output MUST use the stable doctorReportJSON shape under output.Success
    - Plain output MUST render a CHECK | STATUS | DETAIL table
    - defaultDoctorRun MUST wire SSH, manifest store, and HTTP probes without mutating remote state

  OutOfScope:
    - Diagnostic logic and check semantics (owned by setup.Diagnose)
    - Local onboarding and remote bootstrap commands

  Scenario (happy-path): Plain healthy report
    Given a healthy DoctorReport
    When mason doctor runs
    Then stdout shows the diagnostic table and the exit code is zero

  Scenario (happy-path): JSON healthy report
    Given --json and a healthy DoctorReport
    When mason doctor runs
    Then stdout is a success envelope with healthy true and the check list

  Scenario (negative): Failed check
    Given a report with at least one fail check
    When mason doctor runs
    Then the report is rendered and the exit code is non-zero without printing errDoctorUnhealthy

  Scenario (negative): Resolve target failure
    Given defaultDoctorRun cannot resolve a target
    When mason doctor runs
    Then emitError renders the failure and the exit code is non-zero
